From d5df88d83b7c273d5e7c697c7946786c4df34f7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:56:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [DS4.1] Engram host hash: a prefilling request with drafts is
 left to the GPU

The scheduler pads a prompt with one token left to the verification width
with placeholder drafts, so a request can be prefilling and verifying at
once. _early_engram_ids raised on it and stopped the engine (spark-ds41f
#677). Adaptive verification places only the verifying requests' rows on
the GPU; a request after them starts at the host's row. The host now
hashes the prefill rows of requests without drafts and leaves a drafted
request's rows UNKNOWN for the GPU; drafts out of order leave the whole
step to the GPU instead of raising.
